{"slug": "act-of-faith", "nyt_id": 1015784, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1015784-act-of-faith", "name": "Act of Faith", "author": "Robert Simonson", "description": "This dark winter cocktail from Dan Greenbaum, who has mixed drinks at The Beagle in the East Village and Attaboy on the Lower East Side, pairs sweet Pedro Ximénez sherry with two kinds of rum and a sizable dose of Angostura bitters, which adds spice elements. The mixture comes on like a rich, rum old-fashioned, the forthright flavors of the rum, sherry and bitters intertwined in a fruitcake-like medley of clove, allspice, nuts, molasses and dried fruits. It’s a nightcap, to be sure, made to accompany dessert at your holiday feast.", "servings": {"text": "1 drink", "min": 1, "max": 1, "yield_type": "other"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": null, "raw": {}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 ½ ounces Jamaican rum, preferably Appleton Reserve", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "unit": "oz", "item": "jamaican rum", "preparation": "preferably Appleton Reserve", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "½ ounce PX sherry", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "oz", "item": "px sherry", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "½ ounce blackstrap rum, such as Cruzan or Gosling’s", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "oz", "item": "blackstrap rum", "preparation": "such as Cruzan or Gosling’s", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "¼ ounce Angostura bitters", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "oz", "item": "angostura bitters", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "Orange twist, for garnish", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "orange twist", "preparation": "for garnish", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "None"}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 171.0, "protein_g": 0.1, "carbohydrates_g": 2.2, "fat_g": null, 